    <system:String x:Key="Str_AboutText">MeshForge — a tool for processing 3D scans.

Features: hole filling, tessellation (subdivision and QEM decimation), color texturing from a photo, mesh cleanup, Laplacian smoothing, auto-orient to the flattest surface, basic transformations.

Formats: import OBJ / STL / PLY (ASCII) / XYZ, export OBJ / STL / PLY / XYZ.

Version 1 limitations: point cloud (triangle-free) tessellation uses a 2.5D projection method — it works well for a single scan pass, not a full 360° reconstruction. PLY import supports the ASCII variant only. Texturing is projection mapping (planar/cylindrical/spherical) from a single photo, not full multi-view photogrammetry.</system:String>
